    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0430" n="318" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg318"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 511.4A1/915.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Hibben to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The
                            Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-11-02"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">November 2, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 437.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegram of the 28th
                        ultimo<anchor n="1" xml:id="d305-f1"/> relating to an intimation from the
                    minister for foreign affairs in regard to the date for the opening of the
                    International Opium Confernce, and to my <pb facs="0431" n="319" xml:id="pg319"
                    /> cablegram of to-day’s date,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d305-f2"/> I have the honor
                    to inclose herewith a copy and translation of a note, just received, from Mr.
                    Van Swinderin, in which he advises me that the Netherlands Government proposes
                    Wednesday, the 30th of May, 1911, as the date for the meeting of the conference
                    in question.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paxton Hibben.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d305-a1.xml" xpointer="d305-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
